puffy
-----

Dotfiles for OpenBSD.

doas

    $ echo "permit persist USERNAME" > /etc/doas.conf

apmd

    $ doas rcctl enable apmd
    $ doas rcctl set apmd flags -A
    $ doas rcctl start apmd

xenodm

    $ doas rcctl enable xenodm
    $ doas rcctl start xenodm
    $ doas vi /etc/X11/xenodm/Xsetup_0

        /usr/X11R6/bin/xsetroot -solid "#babbbd"

login class

    $ doas usermod -L staff USERNAME

sysctl.conf

    Run scripts/sysctlconf.sh and add to /etc/sysctl.conf as needed.

install intel firmware

    $ doas fw_update intel

snapshots

    /etc/installurl

        https://cdn.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD

    /etc/profile

        export PKG_PATH="https://cdn.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/snapshots/packages/amd64/"

    Upgrade base system

        $ doas sysupgrade -s

    Update packages

        $ doas pkg_add -u

burp

    Download JAR v 1.7.36
        https://portswigger.net/burp/releases/professional-community-1-7-36

    Include jdk-1.8.0 in path
        /usr/local/jdk-1.8.0/bin/

npm

    $ mkdir ~/.npm-global
    $ npm config set prefix "$HOME/.npm-global"


firefox

    General performance:

        about:config

            layers.acceleration.force-enabled -> true
            webgl.disabled -> true (if needed)

    VA-API (for Intel; enabled by default for AMD?):

        Check output of `vainfo` (libva-utils).

        about:support

            Check if "Compositing" ids "WebRender (Software)", in which case
            changes are necessary.

            Verify if "HARDWARE_VIDEO_DECODING" is available. I will likely be
            disabled for user.

        about:config

            gfx.webrender.software -> false
            media.hardware-video-decoding.enabled -> true
            gfx.webrender.all -> true
